<style>
  @page {
    size: A4;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .page {
    width: 794px;
    height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden;
    page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  .page:last-child {
    page-break-after: auto;
  }
  h1, h2, h3 {
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  .header-info {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    font-size: 10pt;
  }
  .chart-container {
    margin-top: 30px;
  }
  .bar-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    font-size: 10pt;
  }
  .label {
    width: 30%;
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
  }
  .bar-wrapper {
    flex-grow: 1;
    height: 15px;
    background-color: #eee;
    border-radius: 3px;
    position: relative;
    margin-right: 10px;
  }
  .bar {
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: 3px;
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
  }
  .value-label {
    width: 50px;
    text-align: right;
    font-size: 10pt;
  }
  .legend {
    display: flex;
    gap: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 10pt;
  }
  .legend-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .legend-color {
    width: 15px;
    height: 15px;
    margin-right: 5px;
  }
  .table-container {
    margin-top: 30px;
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 10pt;
  }
  th, td {
    padding: 8px 0;
    text-align: left;
  }
  th {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc;
  }
  .footer-text {
    font-size: 8pt;
    margin-top: 40px;
    text-align: right;
  }
  .section-title {
    font-size: 16pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .list-item {
    margin-bottom: 15px;
    font-size: 11pt;
  }
  .list-item ul {
    list-style-type: disc;
    margin-left: 20px;
    padding-left: 0;
  }
  .list-item li {
    margin-bottom: 5px;
  }
</style>

<div class="page">
  <div class="header-info">
    <div><span data-field="institution_name">{{ institution_name }}</span></div>
    <div>code(4)lib 2020</div>
  </div>

  <h1 class="section-title">Web Pageviews and Aeon Requests</h1>
  <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 10pt;">(RBML/UA only. Shown in log scale)</p>

  <div class="legend">
    <div class="legend-item">
      <div class="legend-color" style="background-color: #1f77b4;"></div>
      Pageviews
    </div>
    <div class="legend-item">
      <div class="legend-color" style="background-color: #ff7f0e;"></div>
      2019 requests
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-container">
    {% for item in web_data %}
    <div class="bar-row">
      <div class="label"><span data-field="web_data[{{ loop.index0 }}].name">{{ item.name }}</span></div>
      <div class="bar-wrapper">
        <div class="bar" style="width: {{ item.pageviews }}%; background-color: #1f77b4;"></div>
        <div class="bar" style="width: {{ item.requests }}%; background-color: #ff7f0e;"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="value-label">{{ item.pageviews }}</div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <div class="footer-text">25</div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="header-info">
    <div><span data-field="institution_name">{{ institution_name }}</span></div>
    <div>code(4)lib 2020</div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="section-title">Ratio of Pageviews per DSC Character*</h2>

  <div class="table-container">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th><span data-field="table_data[{{ 0 }}].name">{{ table_data[0].name }}</span></th>
          <th><span data-field="table_data[{{ 0 }}].pageviews">{{ table_data[0].pageviews }}</span></th>
          <th><span data-field="table_data[{{ 0 }}].ratio">{{ table_data[0].ratio }}</span></th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for item in table_data %}
        <tr>
          <td><span data-field="table_data[{{ loop.index0 }}].name">{{ item.name }}</span></td>
          <td><span data-field="table_data[{{ loop.index0 }}].pageviews">{{ item.pageviews }}</span></td>
          <td><span data-field="table_data[{{ loop.index0 }}].ratio">{{ item.ratio }}</span></td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="footer-text">* Excludes collections with no EAD component description (e.g., PDF finding aids).</p>

  <div class="footer-text" style="margin-top: 50px;">26</div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 class="section-title">The Case for Google Data Studio for Digital Libraries</h1>

  <p style="font-size: 11pt;">Probably not for everyone. Not as powerful as Tableau or other paid apps.</p>

  <p style="font-size: 11pt; margin-top: 20px;">Best fit is for contexts where you:</p>
  <ul>
    {% for point in google_studio_benefits %}
    <li class="list-item">{{ point }}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>

  <p style="font-size: 11pt; margin-top: 20px;">It may hit a “sweet spot” between more robust ($) applications like Tableau, programming your own (Plotly, Bokeh, etc.), and using limited out-of-the-box reporting tools that come with your existing library software/services.</p>

  <div class="footer-text" style="margin-top: 50px;">27</div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 class="section-title">Thank you!</h1>

  <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 40px;">Demo report links:</p>
  <ul style="list-style-type: disc;">
    <li class="list-item"><span data-field="demo_link_1">{{ demo_link_1 }}</span></li>
    <li class="list-item"><span data-field="demo_link_2">{{ demo_link_2 }}</span></li>
  </ul>

  <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 30px;">Contact:</p>
  <div style="font-size: 11pt;">
    <p><span data-field="contact_name">{{ contact_name }}</span></p>
    <p><span data-field="contact_title">{{ contact_title }}</span></p>
    <p><span data-field="contact_institution">{{ contact_institution }}</span></p>
    <p><span data-field="contact_email">{{ contact_email }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="footer-text" style="margin-top: 50px;">28</div>
</div></body>
</html>